      "text": "To find the ratio of the volume of a cube with edge length six inches to the volume of a cube with edge length one foot, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the volume of the first cube (with an edge length of six inches).\n2. Calculate the volume of the second cube (with an edge length of one foot, which is equivalent to 12 inches).\n3. Find the ratio of these two volumes.\n\nFirst, we calculate the volume of the cube with an edge length of six inches. The volume V of a cube with edge length a is given by the formula:\n\n\\[ V = a^3 \\]\n\nSo, for a cube with edge length 6 inches:\n\n\\[ V_1 = 6^3 = 6 \\times 6 \\times 6 \\]\n\nNext, we calculate the volume of the cube with an edge length of one foot. This is equivalent to 12 inches, so:\n\n\\[ V_2 = 12^3 \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the ratio of the volumes:\n\n\\[ \\text{Ratio} = \\frac{V_1}{V_2} = \\frac{6^3}{12^3} = \\frac{216}{1728} \\]\n\nWe can simplify the fraction \\(\\frac{216}{1728}\\) by dividing both the numerator and the denominator by their greatest common divisor, which is 216:\n\n\\[ \\frac{216 \\div 216}{1728 \\div 216} = \\frac{1}{8} \\]\n\nSo, the ratio of the volume of the cube with edge length six inches to the volume of the cube with edge length one foot is \\(\\frac{1}{8}\\).\n\nWe can confirm this with Python code. Let's write the code to verify this.\n```python\n# Define the edge lengths\nedge_length_1 = 6  # inches\nedge_length_2 = 12  # inches\n\n# Calculate the volumes\nvolume_1 = edge_length_1 ** 3\nvolume_2 = edge_length_2 ** 3\n\n# Calculate the ratio\nratio = volume_1 / volume_2\n\n# Represent the ratio as a fraction in simplest form\nfrom fractions import Fraction\nratio_fraction = Fraction(volume_1, volume_2).limit_denominator()\n\nprint(((ratio, ratio_fraction)))\n```\n```output\n(0.125, Fraction(1, 8))\n```\nThe ratio of the volume of a cube with edge length six inches to the volume of a cube with edge length one foot is \\(\\frac{1}{8}\\).\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{1}{8}}\n\\]",
