    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the ratio of the volume of a cube with an edge length of six inches to the volume of a cube with an edge length of one foot, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Calculate the volume of each cube:**\n\n   - **Volume of the cube with edge length six inches:**\n     The formula for the volume \\( V \\) of a cube is given by:\n     \\[\n     V = s^3\n     \\]\n     where \\( s \\) is the edge length of the cube.\n\n     For the cube with edge length six inches:\n     \\[\n     s = 6 \\text{ inches}\n     \\]\n     So, the volume \\( V_1 \\) is:\n     \\[\n     V_1 = 6^3 = 6 \\times 6 \\times 6 = 216 \\text{ cubic inches}\n     \\]\n\n   - **Volume of the cube with edge length one foot:**\n     Since 1 foot is equal to 12 inches, the edge length in inches is:\n     \\[\n     s = 12 \\text{ inches}\n     \\]\n     So, the volume \\( V_2 \\) is:\n     \\[\n     V_2 = 12^3 = 12 \\times 12 \\times 12 = 1728 \\text{ cubic inches}\n     \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the ratio of the volumes:**\n\n   The ratio of the volume of the smaller cube to the larger cube is given by:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Ratio} = \\frac{V_1}{V_2}\n   \\]\n\n   Substituting the values we found:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Ratio} = \\frac{216}{1728}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Simplify the fraction:**\n\n   To simplify \\(\\frac{216}{1728}\\), we need to find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 216 and 1728. \n\n   - The prime factorization of 216:\n     \\[\n     216 = 2^3 \\times 3^3\n     \\]\n\n   - The prime factorization of 1728:\n     \\[\n     1728 = 2^6 \\times 3^3\n     \\]\n\n   The common factors are \\(2^3 \\times 3 = 24\\), so we divide both the numerator and the denominator by 24:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{216 \\div 24}{1728 \\div 24} = \\frac{9}{72}\n   \\]\n\n   Next, we can simplify \\(\\frac{9}{72}\\):\n   \\[\n   \\frac{9 \\div 9}{72 \\div 9} = \\frac{1}{8}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the ratio of the volume of the cube with edge length six inches to the volume of the cube with edge length one foot is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{1}{8}}\n\\]",
